<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the June 6-8 weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. on Sunday. Final data will be issued on Monday.</p>
<p> 1 (*) Con Air ................................. $25.5 million</p>
<p> 2 (1) The Lost World: Jurassic Park ........... $18.5 million</p>
<p> 3 (2) Addicted To Love ........................  $3.8 million</p>
<p> 4 (*) Buddy ...................................  $3.7 million</p>
<p> 5 (3) Gone Fishin' ............................  $3.1 million</p>
<p> 6 (4) Trial and Error .........................  $2.7 million</p>
<p> 7 (7) Austin Powers ...........................  $2.4 million</p>
<p> 8 (5) The Fifth Element .......................  $2.2 million</p>
<p> 9 (6) Breakdown ...............................  $1.9 million</p>
<p> 10(8) Liar Liar ...............................  $1.2 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parentheses, and * stands for new release.</p>
<p>&quot;Con Air&quot; and &quot;Gone Fishin'&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co..</p>
<p>&quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; and &quot;Liar Liar&quot; are released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Addicted To Love&quot; is released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;The Fifth Element&quot; and &quot;Buddy&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Trial and Error&quot; and &quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery&quot; are released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
<p>&quot;Breakdown&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
</text>
